> How do I create an interaction variable using the indProd function from semTools when my moderator is a second-order latent variable?

This is not what the product-indicator method was designed to do.  The easiest thing to do would be to create subscale scores for each (latent) indicator of your higher-order factor, so that its indicators can be manifest instead of latent, so product-indicator methods become applicable.  This would consistent with facet parceling:

https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3909043/

